This package is a new extraction of Linux-visible socket-address, ancillary
data, and netlink ABI policy designed for TheKernel and distributed under
Apache-2.0. It is not a port of any upstream file: no Linux source file was
translated, adapted, or restructured here.

Linux sources were consulted to understand observable sockaddr bounds
checking, socket option and backlog semantics, UNIX and packet socket
admission, rtnetlink and netlink multicast group contracts, and the
sendmsg/recvmsg data-length rules. No other upstream (FreeBSD, NetBSD,
Asterinas, musl) was consulted for this package.

Copied text: Linux C is quoted verbatim in Rust doc comments as the
observable-semantics authority. Measured against the Linux 7.2.3 tree with
`scripts/ci/scan_linux_excerpts.py` (whitespace-normalised lines of >= 40
characters inside fenced code blocks, matched line for line): 15 lines across
11 blocks in 2 files - 7 blocks holding 11 lines in `src/lib.rs`, 4 blocks
holding 4 lines in `src/msg.rs`. At the inclusive >= 25-character threshold the
same 11 blocks hold 24 lines (18 in `src/lib.rs`, 6 in `src/msg.rs`); no block is
new at that threshold, so the 9 extra lines are short ones - `case` labels and
two-line guards - inside hunks the 40-character scan already counted.

The cited hunks are `net/socket.c:251-252`, `net/core/sock.c:686-701`,
`:641-643`, `:436-453`, `net/unix/af_unix.c:1468-1470`,
`net/core/rtnetlink.c:7109-7112`, `net/netlink/af_netlink.c:1872-1873`,
`:1218-1224` and, in the prose above that block, `:1389-1407` in `src/lib.rs`, and
`net/packet/af_packet.c:3452-3454`, `net/ipv4/tcp.c:2680-2682`, `:1483-1485`
and `include/net/sock.h:2751-2753` in `src/msg.rs` (the prose above that block
cites the enclosing `sock_rcvlowat()` at `:2749-2754`). Every block carries an
inline marker line, "Excerpt: Linux v7.2.3 <file>:<lines> - GPL-2.0-only,
(C) The Linux Kernel Authors", in addition to the file-and-line citation its
surrounding prose already gave: 12 marker lines over the 11 counted blocks, the
extra one at `src/lib.rs:1053`, whose `af_netlink.c:1872-1873` hunk is made of
lines under 25 characters and is therefore disclosed by its marker rather than
by a scan count.

Those fragments are GPL-2.0-only, (C) The Linux Kernel Authors. They are
comment text, not code: no Linux code is linked, assembled, or compiled into
this package, and the Apache-2.0 grant above does not extend to the quoted
text. Nothing else in this package reproduces upstream source text. See
`docs/upstream-provenance.md` for the full per-file index.
